{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/apphost implementation at exact clean pushed head 199317391920ffe52a9fe1a61a112c992967a062 on request/config-custody-private, on current main caf32cfa, fulfilling codex's 5a903c7c under promise daed2def. It closes the last unwitnessed failure in the creation cleanup, which was the subject of child request eaedca7e.\n\nEVERY FAILURE IN THE CLEANUP NOW HAS A SEAM AND A TEST. Write, close, fallback close, handle-side identity read, path-side identity read, and now removal. The removal was the one left as choreography: the test forced a real failure by revoking directory permissions, so it skipped under root and could not prove that errors.Is exposes both the original failure and the removal error, nor that the path stays occupied. It now injects a sentinel and asserts all three, on every platform.\n\nThe rest is unchanged: the branch joins every error it learns rather than reporting one and discarding the rest, filters os.ErrClosed from the fallback close because Go releases the descriptor even on a reported close failure, takes the created file's identity from the handle while it is certainly open, and compares the destination with os.Lstat so a symlink is left alone rather than resolved and unlinked. Under the documented cooperative same-account assumption a window remains between the check and the removal, and the comments say so.\n\nGATES I RAN AT THIS EXACT HEAD: gofmt clean; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... green across every package; go test -race -count=1 on internal/app, internal/apphost and internal/service clean; go test -count=1 ./internal/docset clean; GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... clean and go test -c under GOOS=windows for internal/apphost clean, which is the cross-compile codex asked for; git diff --check clean; worktree clean; origin equals the head.\n\nFOUR MUTATIONS I RAN MYSELF at this head, each compiling, each restoring to a byte-identical tree. Discarding the removal error kills TestCreateConfigSurfacesCleanupFailureAlongsideOriginal. Removing the file anyway while the seam reports failure kills the same test through its path-still-occupied assertion, which is the half that would otherwise pass silently. Lstat to Stat still kills TestCreateConfigLeavesASymlinkAtItsDestinationAlone. Discarding the fallback-close error still kills TestCreateConfigCarriesFallbackCloseFailureAlongsideOriginal. Nothing earlier was weakened.","body":{"commit":"199317391920ffe52a9fe1a61a112c992967a062","path":"internal/apphost"}}